&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;Postman is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, national origin, age, marital status, protected veteran status, or disability status. Headhunters and recruitment agencies may not submit resumes/CVs through this website or directly to managers. Postman does not accept unsolicited headhunter and agency resumes. Postman will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Postman is the world’s leading API platform, used by more than 45 million+ developers and 500,000 organizations, including 98% of the Fortune 500. Postman is helping developers and professionals across the globe build the API-first world by simplifying each step of the API lifecycle and streamlining collaboration—enabling users to create better APIs, faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company is headquartered in San Francisco and has offices in Boston, New York, Austin, Tokyo, London, and Bangalore - where Postman was founded. Postman is privately held, with funding from Battery Ventures, BOND, Coatue, CRV, Insight Partners, and Nexus Venture Partners. Learn more at postman.com or connect with Postman on X via @getpostman.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P.S: We highly recommend reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://api-first-world.com/&quot;&gt;The &quot;API-First World&quot; graphic novel&lt;/a&gt; to understand the bigger picture and our vision at Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Postman is the world’s leading API platform, used by millions of developers and thousands of organizations to design, build, test, and operate APIs that power modern software. As APIs become the backbone of digital business and AI-driven systems, enterprises rely on Postman to ensure the quality, security, and governance of the APIs that run their most critical applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Financial services has emerged as one of Postman’s fastest-growing and most strategic customer segments. Banks and financial infrastructure providers are increasingly building platform businesses powered by APIs, enabling everything from payments and open banking to embedded finance and AI-driven services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To accelerate our momentum in this market, we are launching our first vertical-focused sales team dedicated to financial services.&amp;nbsp;We are looking for a&amp;nbsp;Head of Financial Services, Americas to build and lead this effort.&amp;nbsp;This is a senior leadership role reporting directly to the Chief Revenue Officer, based on the East Coast (preferably New York City or Boston).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead Postman’s enterprise sales team for the banking and financial services industry. This team will focus on both expanding relationships with our largest existing financial services customers and landing new enterprise accounts across the sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Financial institutions depend on APIs for secure money movement, partner integrations, and customer-facing digital experiences. These use cases demand exceptional API quality, governance, and security, making Postman a critical platform for engineering teams across the industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build and lead a team of Strategic Account Executives and Key Account Directors focused on the largest banks, insurance and financial infrastructure companies in the world. As well as midsize and regional banks across the US, Canada and LATAM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond leading the team, you will act as the executive face of Postman within the financial services ecosystem, working directly with customers, representing Postman at industry events, and helping shape how our platform evolves to meet the needs of this market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead Postman’s Financial Services Enterprise Sales team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive revenue growth across global banks, major insurance companies, payments networks, and regional financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own both customer expansion and new logo acquisition across the segment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead from the front, spending significant time in the field with customers and prospects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop trusted relationships with engineering, platform, and technology leadership within financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with internal Product and Engineering teams to ensure Postman’s platform evolves to meet the needs of financial services customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Postman at industry conferences, events, and publications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate as the GM of this segment, setting strategy and driving outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop, and lead a high-performing team of enterprise sellers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of enterprise software sales experience, with significant experience in financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success selling into engineering and technology leadership at large banks and financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading strategic enterprise sales teams and closing complex multi-million-dollar deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the financial services technology landscape, including banking platforms, fintech infrastructure, and modern API ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating as both a strategic leader and hands-on seller&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence with the ability to represent Postman with credibility in industry forums&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder who thrives in creating new go-to-market motions and vertical strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about modern software development, APIs, and the future of platform businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4036&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What Else?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;In addition to Postman&#39;s pay-on-performance philosophy, and a flexible schedule working with a fun, collaborative team, Postman offers a comprehensive set of benefits, including full medical coverage, flexible PTO, wellness reimbursement, and a monthly lunch stipend. Along with that, our wellness programs will help you stay in the best of your physical and mental health. Our frequent and fascinating team-building events will keep you connected, while our donation-matching program can support the causes you care about. We’re building a long-term company with an inclusive culture where everyone can be the best version of themselves.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;At Postman we value in person collaboration. We are in office 5 days a week for all roles based out of our hubs in San Francisco Bay Area, Boston, Austin, New York City, Tokyo and London. For roles based in Bangalore, employees currently work in the office three days a week and will transition to five days per week by the end of the year. We were thoughtful in our approach which is based on collaboration and grounded in feedback from our workforce, leadership team, and peers. The benefits of our in office model will be shared knowledge, brainstorming sessions, communication, and building trust in-person that cannot be replicated via zoom.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3620&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Our Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3633&quot;&gt;At Postman, we create with the same curiosity that we see in our users. We value transparency and honest communication about not only successes, but also failures. In our work, we focus on specific goals that add up to a larger vision. Our inclusive work culture ensures that everyone is valued equally as important pieces of our final product. We are dedicated to delivering the best products we can.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;Postman is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, national origin, age, marital status, protected veteran status, or disability status. Headhunters and recruitment agencies may not submit resumes/CVs through this website or directly to managers. Postman does not accept unsolicited headhunter and agency resumes. Postman will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Postman is the world’s leading API platform, used by more than 45 million+ developers and 500,000 organizations, including 98% of the Fortune 500. Postman is helping developers and professionals across the globe build the API-first world by simplifying each step of the API lifecycle and streamlining collaboration—enabling users to create better APIs, faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company is headquartered in San Francisco and has offices in Boston, New York, Austin, Tokyo, London, and Bangalore - where Postman was founded. Postman is privately held, with funding from Battery Ventures, BOND, Coatue, CRV, Insight Partners, and Nexus Venture Partners. Learn more at postman.com or connect with Postman on X via @getpostman.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P.S: We highly recommend reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://api-first-world.com/&quot;&gt;The &quot;API-First World&quot; graphic novel&lt;/a&gt; to understand the bigger picture and our vision at Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a net new leadership role created to centralize planning that today is spread across teams. Planning processes and data models already exist, but they are fragmented and undocumented. Your job is to bring them together into one centralized planning model, iterate on them, and document and socialize them with stakeholders before they are executed against, so the org plans off a shared, well-understood foundation rather than tribal knowledge. You will own, and lead a team to run, the centralized planning model that connects marketing demand to revenue: the reverse waterfall from MQLs and pipeline by source, through to bookings, customer and logo targets, sales quota and headcount capacity, and territory design. You&#39;ll set the planning strategy, build the operating model, run the planning calendar, and grow the function beneath it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Centralized Planning Model.&lt;/strong&gt; Own the single, connected planning model for GTM. Bring quota planning, capacity planning, headcount planning, and coverage planning onto one shared set of assumptions instead of separate, disconnected plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Iterate, Document &amp;amp; Socialize.&lt;/strong&gt; Take the existing planning processes and data models, refine them, and make them explicit. Document the methodology and assumptions and socialize them with Finance, field leaders, and theater partners so there is alignment and buy-in before execution, not after.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reverse-Waterfall Pipeline &amp;amp; Target Setting.&lt;/strong&gt; Own the reverse waterfall from MQLs and pipeline by source, through bookings and customer/logo targets, so that pipeline targets are derived from revenue goals. Use the same model to size the customer base and downstream capacity needs it implies, giving sales a clear, defensible line from demand to quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quota, Capacity &amp;amp; Headcount Planning.&lt;/strong&gt; Own bottoms-up quota-capacity modeling, sales headcount and ramp assumptions, and the link between capacity and attainable targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Territory &amp;amp; Coverage Design.&lt;/strong&gt; Translate quota-capacity planning into territory and coverage plans in partnership with field leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Annual &amp;amp; In-Year Planning Cycle.&lt;/strong&gt; Design and run Postman&#39;s GTM planning calendar end to end as a program, with clear milestones, owners, inputs, deadlines, and decision points on a predictable cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Theater Partnership.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with the sales ops business partners in each theater so planning assumptions, inputs, and outputs are consistent across regions and the field&#39;s needs are represented in the central plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Alignment &amp;amp; Swimlanes.&lt;/strong&gt; Operate a clear collaboration model with Strategy &amp;amp; Ops (Finance), FP&amp;amp;A, Marketing Ops, Revenue Intelligence, and field leaders, documenting who owns what to remove overlap and close gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead, develop, and grow the Connected Planning team, starting with the Sr. Revenue Intelligence Manager, and raise the planning bar across Field Ops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a builder, a leader, a diplomat, a planner, and above all an innovator. You are a creative ops leader who finds ways to save time, cut through complexity, and build the processes that get all of revops singing from the same sheet of music. You can architect a quota-capacity model yourself, take existing processes and make them rigorous and well documented, run a complex planning cycle as a program with many stakeholders, coach a team to deliver it, and align Finance, Marketing, and Sales leadership on one set of planning assumptions. You think in systems and full funnels, and you bring order to ambiguous, cross-team ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in GTM/Sales Planning, Revenue Operations, or Sales Strategy in high-growth B2B SaaS, including ownership of an annual GTM planning cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up or formalizing a planning function, taking existing processes and data models and making them documented, repeatable, and adopted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional project and program management skills, with a track record of running complex, cross-functional planning cycles to deadline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People-management experience, having built and/or led a planning or rev ops team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in reverse-waterfall and pipeline modeling, quota-capacity and headcount planning, and territory and coverage design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with theater or regional sales ops business partners to drive consistent planning at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Finance/FP&amp;amp;A on target-setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel/Sheets modeling, strong Salesforce, and familiarity with Clari, Xactly, Tableau, or equivalents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence and stakeholder management, able to define swimlanes and drive alignment in a matrixed org.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in San Francisco and able to work in-office 5 days per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems thinker who connects demand, bookings, quota, capacity, and coverage into one centralized plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project and program manager who runs planning cycles to deadline across many stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorous modeler with a bias for clean, defensible, well-documented planning assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trusted cross-functional leader who brings clarity to ambiguous ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People leader who builds and grows high-performing planning teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The reasonably estimated base salary for this role ranges from $225,000 to $280,000, plus a competitive equity package. Actual compensation is based on the candidate&#39;s skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4036&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What Else?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;In addition to Postman&#39;s pay-on-performance philosophy, and a flexible schedule working with a fun, collaborative team, Postman offers a comprehensive set of benefits, including full medical coverage, flexible PTO, wellness reimbursement, and a monthly lunch stipend. Along with that, our wellness programs will help you stay in the best of your physical and mental health. Our frequent and fascinating team-building events will keep you connected, while our donation-matching program can support the causes you care about. We’re building a long-term company with an inclusive culture where everyone can be the best version of themselves.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;At Postman we value in person collaboration. We are in office 5 days a week for all roles based out of our hubs in San Francisco Bay Area, Boston, Austin, New York City, Tokyo and London. For roles based in Bangalore, employees currently work in the office three days a week and will transition to five days per week by the end of the year. We were thoughtful in our approach which is based on collaboration and grounded in feedback from our workforce, leadership team, and peers. The benefits of our in office model will be shared knowledge, brainstorming sessions, communication, and building trust in-person that cannot be replicated via zoom.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3620&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Our Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3633&quot;&gt;At Postman, we create with the same curiosity that we see in our users. We value transparency and honest communication about not only successes, but also failures. In our work, we focus on specific goals that add up to a larger vision. Our inclusive work culture ensures that everyone is valued equally as important pieces of our final product. We are dedicated to delivering the best products we can.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;Postman is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, national origin, age, marital status, protected veteran status, or disability status. Headhunters and recruitment agencies may not submit resumes/CVs through this website or directly to managers. Postman does not accept unsolicited headhunter and agency resumes. Postman will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Postman is the world’s leading API platform, used by more than 45 million+ developers and 500,000 organizations, including 98% of the Fortune 500. Postman is helping developers and professionals across the globe build the API-first world by simplifying each step of the API lifecycle and streamlining collaboration—enabling users to create better APIs, faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company is headquartered in San Francisco and has offices in Boston, New York, Austin, Tokyo, London, and Bangalore - where Postman was founded. Postman is privately held, with funding from Battery Ventures, BOND, Coatue, CRV, Insight Partners, and Nexus Venture Partners. Learn more at postman.com or connect with Postman on X via @getpostman.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P.S: We highly recommend reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://api-first-world.com/&quot;&gt;The &quot;API-First World&quot; graphic novel&lt;/a&gt; to understand the bigger picture and our vision at Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Director/Director, GTM Tools &amp;amp; Technology to own the systems and tooling that power Postman&#39;s entire go-to-market organization. This is a strategic leadership role sitting at the intersection of business operations, systems architecture, and AI innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be the internal product owner for our GTM tech stack — from Salesforce at its core, to every platform that plugs into it, across both pre-sale and post-sale. You&#39;ll define the vision and drive the roadmap for how we use technology and AI to make our GTM teams faster, smarter, and more effective. This role demands both strategic range and operational depth: you&#39;ll partner directly with GTM executives across Sales, Marketing, Customer Success, Professional Services, Revenue Operations, and Finance, while leading a team to deliver on a high bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The standard we&#39;re hiring to is high. We want someone who can architect for where Postman is going, not just maintain what exists — and who will lead meaningfully on AI adoption as a first-class mandate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GTM Systems Strategy &amp;amp; Roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the roadmap for Postman&#39;s GTM tech stack across the full customer lifecycle — from pipeline to renewal and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business needs from Sales, CS, Professional Services, and GTM Ops into scalable system solutions, balancing build vs. buy decisions with long-term architectural coherence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary business systems partner and trusted advisor to GTM leadership — surfacing opportunities, managing tradeoffs, and aligning stakeholders on priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the GTM tools budget; drive ROI accountability across the portfolio and manage vendor relationships, contracts, and renewals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Marketing Ops on the overall GTM platform strategy and AI roadmap, ensuring alignment across the full funnel without duplicating ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Roadmap for GTM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the AI roadmap for the GTM organization in close collaboration with GTM leadership, Engineering, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify the highest-impact opportunities to embed AI and automation across the revenue lifecycle: lead scoring, pipeline forecasting, conversation intelligence, rep productivity, automated enrichment, next-best-action, and customer health signals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with IT, Data Engineering, and Analytics to build the data foundation required for reliable AI outputs — clean, unified, and governed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a repeatable framework for assessing, piloting, and scaling AI tools within the GTM stack, including change management and adoption measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the GTM org&#39;s AI priorities in cross-functional conversations with executive leadership and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pre-Sale Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design, configuration, governance, and continuous improvement of Salesforce Sales Cloud as the system of record for the GTM org.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage integrations across the pre-sale stack (e.g., Outreach/Salesloft, Clari, ZoomInfo, CPQ, Docusign, Ironclad, etc.) ensuring data flows are reliable, clean, and auditable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead system-level support for major GTM initiatives including territory changes, compensation plan rollouts, new product launches, and go-to-market model shifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-Sale Ecosystem&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the systems architecture for Postman&#39;s post-sale teams, including Professional Services Automation (Rocketlane, Certinia, or equivalent), customer service and ticketing (Zendesk, Intercom, Service Cloud, or equivalent), and Customer Success platforms (Gainsight, Catalyst, or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure post-sale systems are well-integrated with Salesforce and the broader GTM data model, enabling a unified view of the customer lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with CS, Professional Services, and Support leadership to continuously improve workflows, automation, and data quality across post-sale tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process &amp;amp; Workflow Automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and eliminate manual, error-prone processes across the lead-to-cash and post-sale lifecycle through automation, smarter tooling, and process redesign.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a low-code/no-code approach to operational efficiency, while knowing when to engage Engineering for more complex builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own documentation, change management, and communication for all system changes affecting the GTM org.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of systems professionals; set direction, grow talent, and build organizational capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of rigor, ownership, and continuous improvement within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and structure the team as Postman&#39;s GTM systems needs evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in business systems, revenue operations technology, or GTM systems roles at high-growth B2B SaaS companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on Salesforce expertise (Sales Cloud); Salesforce Admin certification or equivalent practical depth required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning a GTM tech stack end-to-end — strategy through execution — across both pre-sale and post-sale systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building and delivering multi-year systems roadmaps with measurable business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating and deploying AI and automation tools in a GTM or revenue context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to partner with Engineering as a co-stakeholder on systems and AI initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and developing a team of admins, analysts, and developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication skills — you can translate technical complexity for a CRO and business requirements for an engineering team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce Architect certification (Application Architect, System Architect, or CTA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with iPaaS / integration tools (Workato, MuleSoft, Boomi, or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a developer-focused or PLG (product-led growth) SaaS company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to revenue recognition or finance systems (Zuora, Stripe Billing, NetSuite, or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving systems roadmaps for M&amp;amp;A integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Familiarity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CRM:&lt;/strong&gt; Salesforce Sales Cloud (SOQL, Flow, reports/dashboards)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CPQ:&lt;/strong&gt; Salesforce CPQ, DealHub, or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Outreach, Salesloft, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Revenue Intelligence:&lt;/strong&gt; Clari, Gong, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Enrichment:&lt;/strong&gt; ZoomInfo, Clearbit, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-Sale / PSA:&lt;/strong&gt; Rocketlane, Certinia, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Success:&lt;/strong&gt; Gainsight, Catalyst, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Service:&lt;/strong&gt; Zendesk, Intercom, Service Cloud, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BI / Analytics:&lt;/strong&gt; Tableau, Looker, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Automation&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(collaboration, not ownership):&lt;/em&gt; Marketo, HubSpot, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The reasonably estimated base salary for this role ranges from $230,000 to $290,000, plus a competitive equity package. Actual compensation is based on the candidate&#39;s skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4036&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What Else?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;In addition to Postman&#39;s pay-on-performance philosophy, and a flexible schedule working with a fun, collaborative team, Postman offers a comprehensive set of benefits, including full medical coverage, flexible PTO, wellness reimbursement, and a monthly lunch stipend. Along with that, our wellness programs will help you stay in the best of your physical and mental health. Our frequent and fascinating team-building events will keep you connected, while our donation-matching program can support the causes you care about. We’re building a long-term company with an inclusive culture where everyone can be the best version of themselves.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;At Postman we value in person collaboration. We are in office 5 days a week for all roles based out of our hubs in San Francisco Bay Area, Boston, Austin, New York City, Tokyo and London. For roles based in Bangalore, employees currently work in the office three days a week and will transition to five days per week by the end of the year. We were thoughtful in our approach which is based on collaboration and grounded in feedback from our workforce, leadership team, and peers. The benefits of our in office model will be shared knowledge, brainstorming sessions, communication, and building trust in-person that cannot be replicated via zoom.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3620&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Our Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3633&quot;&gt;At Postman, we create with the same curiosity that we see in our users. We value transparency and honest communication about not only successes, but also failures. In our work, we focus on specific goals that add up to a larger vision. Our inclusive work culture ensures that everyone is valued equally as important pieces of our final product. We are dedicated to delivering the best products we can.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;Postman is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, national origin, age, marital status, protected veteran status, or disability status. Headhunters and recruitment agencies may not submit resumes/CVs through this website or directly to managers. Postman does not accept unsolicited headhunter and agency resumes. Postman will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Postman is the world’s leading API platform, used by more than 45 million+ developers and 500,000 organizations, including 98% of the Fortune 500. Postman is helping developers and professionals across the globe build the API-first world by simplifying each step of the API lifecycle and streamlining collaboration—enabling users to create better APIs, faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company is headquartered in San Francisco and has offices in Boston, New York, Austin, Tokyo, London, and Bangalore - where Postman was founded. Postman is privately held, with funding from Battery Ventures, BOND, Coatue, CRV, Insight Partners, and Nexus Venture Partners. Learn more at postman.com or connect with Postman on X via @getpostman.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P.S: We highly recommend reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://api-first-world.com/&quot;&gt;The &quot;API-First World&quot; graphic novel&lt;/a&gt; to understand the bigger picture and our vision at Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Postman is entering its next phase of growth, with a marketing organization that spans developer audiences, product-led growth, and enterprise go-to-market motions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To support this scale, we are building a &lt;strong&gt;modern marketing infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt; that combines:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;world-class marketing operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a scalable martech ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;lifecycle automation and customer data infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;high-impact creative production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Head of Marketing Operations &amp;amp; Production&lt;/strong&gt; will lead the team responsible for powering this system, and reports directly to the Head of GTM Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will partner closely with Marketing leadership, Sales and Customer Success Operations, GTM Systems, and Postman’s &lt;strong&gt;GTM Strategy and Business Intelligence teams&lt;/strong&gt; to ensure marketing programs translate into measurable revenue impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Technology &amp;amp; Infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define and own Postman’s &lt;strong&gt;marketing technology ecosystem&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement the roadmap for Postman’s martech stack, including automation platforms, enrichment tools, campaign systems, and lifecycle infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure reliable and scalable integration between marketing systems, CRM platforms, and the broader GTM technology ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and optimize the current stack, making decisions on consolidation, new investments, and vendor partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the &lt;strong&gt;GTM Systems team&lt;/strong&gt;, which owns core GTM architecture and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Campaign Operations &amp;amp; Marketing Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the operational platform that allows marketing teams to execute at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your team will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable global campaign launches across developer marketing, product marketing, and demand generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design scalable campaign workflows, segmentation frameworks, and lifecycle automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own lead management, enrichment, and marketing data capture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure marketing teams can focus on strategy while your team powers execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Data &amp;amp; Measurement Infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create the operational foundation for marketing insight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the systems and data capture frameworks that enable clear visibility into pipeline generation, campaign performance, and lifecycle engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Postman’s &lt;strong&gt;GTM Strategy, Data, and other Operations teams&lt;/strong&gt; to ensure marketing data powers strategic insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Demand Generation and Marketing Analytics teams to ensure web, lifecycle, and campaign data capture supports advanced analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI, Automation &amp;amp; Lifecycle Innovation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify opportunities to deploy &lt;strong&gt;automation and AI across marketing workflows&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;lifecycle engagement infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;lead scoring and segmentation frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;personalization and campaign automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;operational improvements that accelerate marketing velocity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Creative Production&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oversee Postman’s &lt;strong&gt;Marketing Creative team&lt;/strong&gt;, responsible for brand execution and creative production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team powers design and creative services for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;product marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;demand generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;developer marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;global campaigns and events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will ensure the creative organization operates as a &lt;strong&gt;high-impact internal production engine&lt;/strong&gt;, enabling marketing teams to move quickly while maintaining strong brand standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the center of Postman’s GTM ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing leadership across Demand Gen, PMM, and DevRel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales Operations and Customer Success Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GTM Systems and data infrastructure teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Postman’s GTM Strategy organization, which drives revenue planning and analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your success will be measured by how effectively marketing strategy translates into scalable operational execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within 12–18 months:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing teams execute campaigns faster and with greater operational precision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Postman’s martech stack is scalable, integrated, and aligned to GTM strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing data provides clear insight into pipeline creation and lifecycle engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative production becomes a high-performing internal service supporting global marketing initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an operator who combines &lt;strong&gt;systems thinking, marketing insight, and operational leadership&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideal candidates will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in marketing operations, marketing infrastructure, or martech leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building marketing systems for high-growth B2B SaaS companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with modern B2B marketing technology ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting hybrid &lt;strong&gt;PLG and enterprise GTM models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building high-performing operational teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional leadership and the ability to influence senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The reasonably estimated base salary for this role ranges from $275,000-$300,000, plus a competitive equity package. Actual compensation is based on the candidate&#39;s skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4036&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What Else?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
