&lt;p&gt;P.S: We highly recommend reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://api-first-world.com/&quot;&gt;The &quot;API-First World&quot; graphic novel&lt;/a&gt; to understand the bigger picture and our vision at Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Head of Services &amp;amp; Success Operations&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Solutions · Reports to Head of GTM Operations · San Francisco, CA (Hybrid) · Full-Time&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Postman&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Postman is the world&#39;s leading API platform, with 45M+ developers and 500K+ organizations — including 98% of the Fortune 500. We run a dual motion: bottoms-up product-led growth and a top-down enterprise sales org. The tension between those two motions — and the opportunity to design the operating model that bridges them — is exactly what makes this role interesting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Customer Solutions Org&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customer Solutions runs four functions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Success&lt;/strong&gt; — developer-forward CSEs; technical depth over relationship management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Services&lt;/strong&gt; — accelerating outcomes through repeatable, monetized programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solutions Engineering&lt;/strong&gt; — technical depth in the sales cycle; handoff design is part of this ops role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Support&lt;/strong&gt; — inbound; health signals that feed risk models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is the operational connective tissue across all four.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The CS Transformation We&#39;re Running&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re moving from a traditional enterprise CS model built on relationship management and QBRs to a developer-forward motion that prioritizes technical depth at the right moments across the full customer lifecycle. This role, in conjunction with GTM leadership, is the architect of that operating model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Drive&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Operating Model &amp;amp; Metrics&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In conjunction with CS, PS, and SE functional leadership, define and socialize the operating model across Customer Solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the measurement framework — onboarding, activation, adoption, value realization, retention, expansion — and the operating rhythm that keeps functional leaders accountable to it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface PS-specific metrics including delivery quality, time to value, attach rate, and margin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Customer Lifecycle Infrastructure&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In conjunction with Sales and CS leadership, design the post-sale handoff model — including Mutual Delivery Plans that surface implementation milestones and role clarity before close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and iterate onboarding playbooks for high-touch enterprise, scaled mid-market, and PLG-originated converting accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop churn mitigation playbooks, expansion triggers, and risk escalation protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the Engagement Manager program concept — scoping the role and designing the model (1:few for enterprise, data-driven for the long tail) — and partner with CS functional leadership on implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;AE Enablement &amp;amp; Renewals Alignment&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Postman&#39;s Account Executives own the full customer lifecycle, including renewal and expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Sales Operations to define clear role-and-responsibility boundaries between AEs, CSEs, and PS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the signal infrastructure that gives AEs actionable intelligence — churn risk, expansion propensity, recommended next action — based on product usage, support trends, and engagement data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat Renewals Operations as a co-owner of the at-risk customer process: align on early warning thresholds, escalation paths, and intervention timing before renewal windows open&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Systems, Tooling &amp;amp; AI&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will not own the GTM systems team, but you will be the primary product manager and demand-side partner for the systems that serve Customer Solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the CS/PS tooling roadmap — Rocketlane (assess whether it scales), CSE tooling, Zendesk for Support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and implement customer health scoring infrastructure, ensuring data flows reliably from product, support, and CRM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and prioritize AI applications in CS and PS workflows — automated health signal interpretation, AI-assisted playbook execution, intelligent ticket routing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a grounded perspective — distinguish high-value AI opportunities from noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in Customer Success Operations, Revenue Operations, or post-sales operations, spanning both CS and PS/Services, with 5+ years in leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of defining operating models, not just executing them — you&#39;ve taken ambiguous org structures and added clarity, metrics, and rhythm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting orgs that run multiple CS models simultaneously: technical/non-technical, high-touch/scaled, PLG-originated and enterprise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong point of view on CS/PS tooling; familiarity with Rocketlane, Zendesk, Gainsight or equivalents a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Influence&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Peer-level conversation with functional VPs (CS, PS, SE) that is credible, challenging, and useful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build a business case for the CRO with motivations and numbers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough cross-company pattern recognition to have a mental model of what good looks like — and the instinct to push back constructively with something better&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The salary range for this role is $250,000-300,000 plus a competitive equity package. Actual compensation is based on the candidate&#39;s skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Competencies&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating model design · Metrics &amp;amp; analytics · Cross-functional credibility · Change leadership · AI fluency · Tooling judgment&lt;/p&gt;
